coder › Done on branch `work/json-flag` (3 commits).

What changed:
- `src/csv.ts` (new): exports `parseCsv(text: string): string[][]`. Splits on `\r?\n`, drops trailing blank line(s), parses each line with quoted-field support (commas inside quotes, `""` → `"`).
- `src/cli.ts`: added `--json` branch — first parsed row is the header; prints `JSON.stringify(arrayOfObjects) + "\n"` with all values strings; empty input (no rows) prints `[]\n`; header with no data rows also prints `[]\n`; a data row whose field count differs from the header returns code 1 with no JSON. Usage line now `usage: csvtool --upper | --count | --json`.
- `src/csv.test.ts` (new) and `src/cli.test.ts`: tests for plain splits, quoted commas, doubled quotes, CRLF, empty input, header-only, basic object output, string values, ragged-row failure.

Decision not in the plan: the exact wording of the ragged-row error line was unspecified (only that it be one line naming the 1-based line number), so I used `error: line N: expected H fields but got G\n` where N is the 1-based input line number (header = line 1).

